[{:adr/actuation-ops [:actuation/dispatch-alert :actuation/authorize-resume :actuation/file-accident-report :actuation/file-periodic-report], :adr/related ["cloud-itonami-isic-4211/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607082700", :adr/commits ["8cad4e0" "7d0694d"], :adr/jurisdictions-covered ["JPN" "USA" "DEU"], :adr/west-managed? false, :adr/west-managed-note "orgs/cloud-itonami/* (the entire ISIC blueprint fleet, ~150 repos including this one) is absent from both manifest/repos.edn :path entries and manifest/west.yml -- confirmed by grep before writing this ADR. No west.yml pin-advance applies to this change.", :adr/repo "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4211", :adr/promoted-from :blueprint, :adr/auto-eligible-rationale "the one actuation op in this build that MAY auto-commit at phase 3 when the governor is clean -- disaster-alert dispatch has the OPPOSITE risk shape from every other actuation event in this fleet (a delayed warning, not an extra one, is the harm to guard against), and is still gated by a HARD check requiring a human-approved :weather/assess stop-work determination already on file before it can fire", :adr/jurisdiction-note "DEU is the EU-jurisdiction proxy, same convention aerospace.facts already established for EASA -- no ISO-3166 alpha-3 code exists for the EU itself", :adr/notification-channels "{:mail {:provider \"Resend\", :transport \"java.net.http, following cloud-itonami.mail's injectable :http-fn convention\"}, :phone {:provider \"Twilio Programmable Voice\", :transport \"outbound call, inline TwiML <Say> -- a real spoken call per the request's \\\"電話\\\", not SMS\"}, :default \"mock-notifier, deterministic, no network -- default everywhere (dev/tests/demo)\"}", :adr/maturity-note "deliberately NOT :implemented -- the Operator Guide's robot-dispatch (panel-placement) slice of the same :construction-governor remains unbuilt; only the disaster/severe-weather safety slice (assess/inspect/alert/resume/report) is covered here", :adr/date "2026-07-08", :adr/auto-eligible-actuation :actuation/dispatch-alert, :adr/promoted-to :partially-implemented, :db/id -1, :adr/repo-note "NOT the same repo as gftdcojp/cloud-itonami (unrelated actor scoped to aircraft-engine certification, initially confused with this one during investigation)", :adr/follow-ups ["kotoba-lang/industry registry.edn entry \"4211\" has stale :repo/:business-id (wrong org, missing isic- infix: gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-4211 vs the real cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4211) and no :maturity field -- left unfixed, separate PR in that repo, decide there how/whether a :partially-implemented tier fits that registry's three-tier (:spec/:blueprint/:implemented) counting invariant before touching it" "robot-dispatch (panel placement etc., Operator Guide Day-in-the-life example) remains a separate, not-yet-implemented slice of the same :construction-governor"], :adr/test-status "59 tests / 238 assertions, clj-kondo lint clean, clojure -M:dev:run demo verified end-to-end", :adr/legal-sources "{\"JPN\" {:basis \"労働安全衛生規則 第522条(work-stoppage)・第655条(post-severe-weather inspection)・第97条(労働者死傷病報告) / 建築基準法 第12条(定期報告)\", :urls [\"https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/347M50002000032\" \"https://www.mlit.go.jp/jutakukentiku/build/jutakukentiku_house_tk_000039.html\"], :threshold-model :quantitative, :threshold \"wind >=10 m/s (10-min avg) OR rainfall >=50 mm/event OR snowfall >=25 cm/event\"}, \"USA\" {:basis \"OSH Act §5(a)(1) General Duty Clause / 29 CFR 1926.20 / 29 CFR 1904\", :urls [\"https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1926/1926.20\" \"https://www.osha.gov/recordkeeping\"], :threshold-model :qualitative, :threshold-note \"no fixed federal numeric trigger -- honestly represented as :qualitative, never fabricated\"}, \"DEU\" {:basis \"Framework Directive 89/391/EEC Art.5 / Construction Sites Directive 92/57/EEC / Baustellenverordnung\", :urls [\"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/ALL/?uri=celex:31992L0057\" \"https://osha.europa.eu/en/legislation/directives/15\"], :threshold-model :qualitative, :threshold-note \"EU directives set a general risk-assessment duty, not a fixed EU-wide numeric trigger -- honestly represented as :qualitative, never fabricated\"}}", :adr/never-auto-actuations [:actuation/authorize-resume :actuation/file-accident-report :actuation/file-periodic-report], :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-4211 disaster/severe-weather safety slice -- Construction Advisor ⊣ Construction Governor"}]